{
  "_readme": [
    "Maps hymn numbers to themes for the Browse by theme section.",
    "Only confirmed thematic indexes go here - a hymn no range covers is left unthemed",
    "rather than lumped into a placeholder bucket. Numbers are inclusive on both ends.",
    "",
    "To add a range: find the section in the printed hymnal, note its first and last",
    "hymn number, and add an entry under that edition's key. Edition keys are the edition",
    "id (CIS-ru, SDAH) or its code (HCASDA).",
    "",
    "A range may carry its own \"name\" to show the theme in that hymnal's own language",
    "(\"Sifa na Kuabudu\") while keeping the shared slug, which is what makes the theme",
    "recognisable across languages. Omit \"name\" to use the canonical English name in",
    "the themes list below.",
    "",
    "After editing: `npm run load:hymns` for the CIS and SDAH editions, `npm run seed` for",
    "HCASDA. Theme counts in the app are scoped to the language you have selected, so a",
    "card shows only that language's hymns.",
    "",
    "Known gap: the CIS files carry more hymns than these indexes cover - dholuo 284-332,",
    "abagusii 216-370 and gikuyu 231-299 are past the last range and stay unthemed until",
    "their section boundaries are supplied."
  ],
